{{Acquisition|*Secondary Encumber can be obtained from [[Mirror Defense]] as a [[Rotation]] C reward. 
*Purchaseable from [[Otak]] in the [[Necralisk]] for 60 {{Resource|Belric Crystal Fragment}} and {{Resource|Rania Crystal Fragment}} each, with a total of 1,260 of each for max rank.
*Possible reward from [[Bounty#Deepmines Bounties|Deepmines Bounties]] from [[Nightcap]].
*Purchaseable from [[Nightcap]] in [[Fortuna]] for 10 {{Resource|Fergolyte}} each, with a total of 210 for max rank, requiring '''Rank 3 - Seeker'''.}}

==Notes==
*Encumber will only apply a max of '''1''' additional status effect per instant of time, similar to a very short cooldown.
**Multishot and Status Chance values over 100% do not bypass this limit, but more multishot does allow more chances of an Encumber proc until one succeeds.
***The average Encumber chance per shot can be calculated by: {{MathText|1 - (1 - 24% {{mul}} min(statusChance, 1)) ^ pelletCount}}
**Hitting multiple targets at the same time will '''only''' allow up to '''one''' proc for only '''one''' of the affected targets per instant.
***Explosions, Hitscan Punch Through ({{Weapon|Twin Kohmak}}), Beam Chains ({{Weapon|Kuva Nukor}}), Multibeams ({{Weapon|Ocucor}}, {{Weapon|Vermisplicer}}) and other simultaneous attacks will only proc up to once on a single target at a time.<ref>{{Ref|title=Arcane Encumber - inconsistent and probably bugged.|year=2023|month=2|day=24|publisher=Warframe Forums|url=https://forums.warframe.com/topic/1340401-arcane-encumber-inconsistent-and-probably-bugged/#comment-12728437|access-date=2023-02-24|extra="Some clarifications for the warrior-scientists in the thread." - [DE]Momaw}}</ref>
***Projectile Multishot ({{Weapon|Detron}}) will only proc once per small target because the projectiles typically strike within Encumber's cooldown.
**<u>Delayed hits</u> such as projectile rebounds ({{Weapon|Cyanex}}), embed delays ({{Weapon|Kompressa}}), and travel time punch-through ({{Weapon|Catchmoon}}) can proc Encumber multiple times per shot because their hits do not always occur at the same time.
**Forced procs ({{Weapon|Hystrix}}) can trigger Encumber.
**As of Update 38.5, [[Exalted Weapon]]s ({{WF|Mesa}}'s {{Weapon|Regulators}}, {{WF|Titania}}'s {{Weapon|Dex Pixia}}, {{WF|Dante}}'s {{Weapon|Noctua}} {{WF|Hildryn}}'s {{Weapon|Balefire Charger}}) '''can''' equip and trigger Encumber.
***Procs from [[Exalted Weapon]]s can activate [[Arcane Enhancement|Arcanes]] and mods that require status effects from abilities, such as {{Arcane|Arcane Impetus}} and {{M|Archon Continuity}}. 
*Random proc is uniformly chosen from the following and is independent from the weapon's damage distribution:
**{{D|Impact}}
**{{D|Puncture}}
**{{D|Slash}}
**{{D|Heat}}
**{{D|Cold}}
**{{D|Electricity}}
**{{D|Toxin}}
**{{D|Blast}}
**{{D|Corrosive}}
**{{D|Magnetic}}
**{{D|Viral}}
**{{D|Gas}}
**{{D|Radiation}}

